---
import { PLATFORM_DESCRIPTION, PLATFORM_NAME } from "astro:env/client";
import ArticleLayout from "#src/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import Link from "#src/components/Link.astro";
import Strong from "#src/components/Strong.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout title="About">
  <hgroup class="bg-linear-45 from-emerald-400 to-zinc-200 bg-clip-text text-center text-transparent">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">About {PLATFORM_NAME}</h1>
    <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl">{PLATFORM_DESCRIPTION}</p>
  </hgroup>

  <p class="mbs-6 text-zinc-400">
    Created by{" "}
    <Link href="https://ssbit01.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Stefan Samson
    </Link>
    , <Strong>profile.rocks</Strong> was born out of a simple need: the ability to create and publish a fully functional micro-page directly
    from any device, from a mobile phone to a computer, without restrictions.
  </p>

  <p class="my-6 text-zinc-400">
    While existing micropage services typically restrict users to basic links and plain text, <Strong>profile.rocks</Strong> was designed to
    support rich Markdown formatting, offering greater flexibility and control over content.
  </p>

  <p class="text-zinc-400">
    Furthermore, unlike the majority of closed-source alternatives on the market, <Strong>profile.rocks</Strong> aims to be open source.
    Future developments will focus on expanding developer tools to support self-hosting, ensuring long-term independence and customization
    for users.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
